title: 'T-007b shipped — atelier trim with parametric cuts and layer-tag isolation'
summary: 'Implemented T-007b end-to-end from spec to working CLI in one focused session. Four commits, no scope creep, no new npm dependencies, 26 new tests added (65/65 in CLI, 528/528 workspace). The pipeline: probe ffmpeg silencedetect filter → ffprobe source duration → run silencedetect → invert silence to speech intervals → buildInitialCuts with default 80ms/120ms padding → mergeWithExisting (preserves user padding on raw-boundary match within 0.5s tolerance, the load-bearing UX invariant) → apply --tighten/--loosen/--cut overrides → resolveOverlaps at silence midpoint → clampBoundaries to [0, duration] → write cuts.json 1.1 → rewriteCutLayers (drop only silence-trim-tagged layers, append fresh clip-trim-N VideoVisual layers with floor/ceil frame rounding). The layer-tag isolation invariant is now proven by test: user-authored layers and other-tagged pipeline outputs (caption, overlay) survive every trim re-run untouched. atelier trim --help dogfooded post-build. Two small pre-existing audit cleanups fixed along the way (unused React import, unused yaml-panel destructure). One pre-existing Shape-narrowing typecheck error in studio/property-panel.ts flagged but not addressed — out of T-007b scope, queued for separate audit.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#video-project'
