commit_chain:
  - 64cb3e0  # parametric CutEntry + rewriteCutLayers + 1.0→1.1 migration (foundation)
  - c3271af  # silence-detect subprocess + cut-model pure functions (core)
  - d2cf1e5  # atelier trim orchestrator + CLI wiring + .purpose + versions (surface)
learnings:
  - 'Building in three layers — foundation (types + migration), core (pure functions), surface (orchestrator + CLI) — let every step ship green with its own tests before depending on it. No commit had to be amended; each was independently verifiable.'
  - 'The advisor''s pre-spec call caught an implicit decision (one VideoVisual per cut vs internal cut-list) and six edge cases that would have shipped silently broken: padding overlap, padding past bounds, sub-frame rounding, re-run preservation behavior, which layers trim touches, recipe-vs-per-cut precedence. Pre-substantive-work advisor calls are now a hard team habit on spec work.'
  - 'parseSilenceDetectStderr deliberately drops unpaired silence_start lines (no following silence_end). This is the right call — ffmpeg can emit a start without an end if the source is truncated. Tests cover this explicitly.'
  - 'ffmpeg silencedetect emits silence_start: -0.123 when audio begins below the noise floor. Parser clamps to 0; tested.'
  - 'mergeWithExisting''s 0.5s tolerance default is a guess that wants empirical validation on real takes. Spec exposes a future --match-tolerance flag if needed.'
  - 'The rewriteCutLayers test that adds a user-overlay layer (tagged "overlay") and verifies it survives the trim rewrite is the load-bearing test for the entire UGC value proposition. If that invariant breaks, every pipeline destroys user work. Keep it.'
  - 'Zero new npm dependencies kept the audit trivial: ffmpeg silencedetect via child_process.spawn (same pattern as render-pipeline.ts), same license posture (subprocess, not linked), no CVE surface beyond what we already accept for the render command.'
  - 'Two pre-existing typecheck errors surfaced during the workspace-wide verification — both unrelated to T-007b. Confirmed via git stash round-trip. Fixed the trivial ones (React unused, colon unused); deferred the real one (Shape narrowing in property-panel) to avoid expanding scope mid-feature.'
